    {"p":"今天是几月几号？ — asking the date","e":"几 means \"which/how many\" in questions. 几月几号 literally asks \"which month, which day\" — the standard way to ask a date.","x":"今天是几月几号？ — What's the date today?"},
    {"p":"number + 月 + number + 号 — giving a date","e":"Chinese goes big to small: month first, then day. 九月五号 = September 5th. In writing you may also see 日 instead of 号.","x":"今天是九月五号。 — Today is September 5th."},
    {"p":"都 — both, all","e":"都 goes after the subject and before the verb, not next to the noun the way English \"both\" does.","x":"我们的生日都在九月。 — Both our birthdays are in September."}
